{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/772928-what-kind-of-beasts-do-exists","id":772928,"title":"What kind of Beasts do exists.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-24T04:07:13-08:00","id":772928,"title":"What kind of Beasts do exists.","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I'm currently working on a Vampire chronicle and I would like to make my players interact with some being which isn't a Vampire but as very strang powers. I was thinking about a Beast, since the interaction would remains minimal but... I know next to nothing about Beasts !<br /> <br /> So could I get a quick summary of what the Beasts are (I remember that early one they were supposed to be born that way, but it is not the case anymore, right ? So I'm a bit confused) and what kind of &quot;families&quot; exists among them. A brief recap would be more than enough.<br /> <br /> Thanks you all in advance !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T14:16:03-08:00","id":773414,"title":"","content":"The first draft of the preview text is still available on Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> It's similar enough to the final draft to use them for crossover play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T15:16:46-08:00","id":773460,"title":"","content":"Beasts go through a thing called the Devouring, it replaced the Homecoming, before moving from human to Beast. Though some Beasts will argue whether this means they were turned into a Beast from a human, if they were always a Beast and this is just coming into their own, if the Horror is merging with the person's soul to make a Beast, or some other thing. Beasts don't have an extensive society, so more often than not Beasts don't have anything like the organizational structures Mages, Vampires, or Werewolves tend to have.<br /> <br /> Beasts tend to be about satisfying their own hungers, some of the Begotten operate on the principle that they should be teaching lessons, others don't care about lessons and just want to feed. A Beast's inner Horror gives no crap about whether or not your actions led to a lesson to anyone or not so long as it gets to eat in the end. The Hungers are not tied to a specific family though Beasts generally have a specific flavor of the hunger they indulge in.<br /> <br /> As far as the Hungers go you have prey, hoard, power, punishment, and ruin. Generally speaking a Beast's classification will at least partially be what kind of hunger they have, so you'll have predators, collectors, tyrants, nemesis, and ravagers. The families are more divided by archetype than specific monsters in it though families have iconic monsters it isn't unheard of for their to be a specific monster in more than one family.<br /> <br /> Anakim are hopelessness essentially an Anakim gives off the idea of a nigh unstoppable force whether intellectually or physically. Think giants, trolls, or cyclops.<br /> <br /> The Eshmaki are darkness you know that thing where the problem isn't fighting the monster its that either don't know its there, or you can't find it until its ripped out your Achilles tendon. This doesn't mean they're weak, but a large part of their fear is that unknowing thing. The baku and Grendel are iconic monsters for this family.<br /> <br /> The Makara are fear of the depths obviously drowning is a simple on, but it can also apply to just having people be overwhelmed by just too many things, or things coming back that should be long gone. Some iconics are the kraken, leviathan, sirens and I do so love <i>J\u00f6rmungandr.</i><br /> <br /> The Namtaru are revulsion think those things that people don't like to look at or think about. For Namtaru think that person in HR that no one wants to deal with not because they do anything inappropriate or wrong, but something about them just unnerves or scares people enough that anyone else in HR is preferable to dealing with this person. You have Medusa as an icon here, as well Kishi, and I always include the worm that walks as an example.<br /> <br /> The Ugallu are exposure. For phenotype the Ugallu tend to be flying monsters, but on the other aspect the Ugallu is just being exposed. As the book puts it think the nightmare where you show up to work or school in your underwear only instead of it only being you aware of it everyone in the dream is aware of it and you can't find anywhere to hide. More often than not you'll be looking at flying monsters when you want an Ugallu.<br /> <br /> As far as specific Horrors go well we list mythological monsters, but there is no rule against more modern ones and you can always create custom horrors like the all seeing web spider that was worked on on the board.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T00:01:57-08:00","id":773692,"title":"","content":"Thanks, both of you ! If I remember well, the Beasts tend to see the other monsters as a sort of Family. So I guess they can make some serious bargains if need be for both sides ? I think a Eshmaki collector could be of use in my chronicle (at a very personal level for my players). If a bBeast is a collector, can it be of knowledge ? And can it enter the minds of Vampires if they let them do so ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T01:08:35-08:00","id":773720,"title":"","content":"Knowledge is perfectly acceptable. However, Beasts are living nightmares so each time the character feeds through learning someone must suffer from it. They can't just break into someone's house, read through their documents and leave without a trace. They must leave marks of their presence, take the files while the owner watches or learn something that could destroy a person and then let them know it.<br /> <br /> Considering their connection to the Primordial Dream, dreamwalking sounds like something Beasts should be able to do. I don't remember if the book says that, though. You could find or create a mind-delving power if you want to. However, all powers are violations in one way or another. They work because the target wouldn't want them to. An appropriate power would be learning what the target fears losing most, or what they are most ashamed of.<br /> <br /> You should give a look to the Nightmares and Atavisms (Beast powers), particularly Kinship Nightmares. The latter easily explain what Beasts get from befriending other monsters. Consider &quot;We Know All Your Secrets&quot; Kinship Nightmare and &quot;Needs Must&quot;, &quot;Mimir's Wisdom&quot;, &quot;Eye of Heaven&quot; Atavisms. Most of them involve information gathering and could be very fitting for the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T01:59:42-08:00","id":773749,"title":"","content":"Oh, I totally planned my players to suffer for the knowledge they may get from her. After all, it wouldn't be a bargain otherwise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T05:14:39-08:00","id":773839,"title":"","content":"It's not exactly what I meant. Beasts victimize Mortals to feed their Hungers. It's something they both need and want to do, so your Collector will likely have some very unpleasant investigation techniques, leaving many shaken humans in his wake. Beasts often come up with justifications for their actions. Teaching their victims or society life lessons through fear is a popular one. Other ones might include punishing the wicked, mad artistry or even simple hedonism. If a Beast truly believes their reasons they can apply them in other situations. So, if the Beasts torments a Vampire it won't be in order to feed. They will have another purpose. This is why you need to decide what the Beast believes and how does it affect their behavior.<br /> <br /> An information broker supplying reliable information to Mortals and Monsters alike, but known for making them go through hell in the process is a promising character concept. You just need to decide what the Beast wants to accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T07:25:49-08:00","id":773941,"title":"","content":"Well, the idea I have is the following :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There was one before the Romans. Some says that it was even there before the Tectosages, but what interest would have it had with no secrets to collect but the howling of the wind and the whispers of the tree ? Yes, it probably came with the Celts... or maybe they came for it. It doesn't really matter anymore. The first Haunts in the city made a pact with it, or perhaps one of its ancestors. Why did the Mehket shunned it when they were there before the Roman Vampires ? Perhaps because they were too alike. What secrets could it learn from them that it didn't already knew ? And the Gangrels were to feral and kept their secrets for themselves, with claws and fangs.<br /> <br /> The Haunts, however, needed secrets. They needed it to carve a place for themselves and so they made a Temple for it, deep, deep, below the buzzing streets of Tolosa. The conditions of the Pact are unknown to the outsiders, but what is known by all is that when one need a certain knowledge, he can obtain it by visiting the Nosferatu. Then, they'll go talk to it... or they'll send to it the ones who seek answers. And the Beast will always give answers, at the price of other knowledge, and its watchful eyes on the back of those who came before it. But it is no mere broker. It watches us all, in the end, and when one deserves absolute truth, it bring it to him. The Haunts have a saying : &quot;The one who seek absolute truth is a fool. It will let him only a consumed husk, for its light is too bright to not harm&quot;. They know what they're talking about.<br /> <br /> Why do I tell you this ? Well, you see, all who reveals their existence are to be killed. I'll face the sun now instead of letting it have its way with me. But you... you've been a nuisance for me during decades. And now it will come to you too. Your carefree nights are over, my childe. </div> </div> </div>Basically, the Beast would act as a Judge. Those it deems corrupt, who like to pretend that they are better than they are, it destroy. Maybe it will reveal to the world their dirty secrets and leave them in jail or worse; perhaps they'll end mentally impaired if she choose to enforce upon her the layers of white lies and delusion that we has people often keep to reassure us. What she feed upon is the instant of pure and unadulterated terror that its victims feels when their lives collapse around them. It works with all the denizens of the World of Darkness, but it has put in place a very strict set of rules. Obviously, there is a lot of mysteries surrounding it, but that's what I want. I want my players to feel some personal horror in the course of the chronicle, since so far only one truly endured it during his Prologue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 11-25-2015, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:49:41-08:00","id":774010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/772928-what-kind-of-beasts-do-exists?p=773941#post773941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the idea I have is the following :<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, the Beast would act as a Judge. Those it deems corrupt, who like to pretend that they are better than they are, it destroy. Maybe it will reveal to the world their dirty secrets and leave them in jail worse; perhaps they'll end mentally impaired if she choose to enforce upon her the layers of white lies and delusion that we has people often keep to reassure us. What she feed upon is the instant of pure and unadulterated that its victims feels when their lives collapse around them. It works with all the denizens of the World of Darkness, but it has put in place a very strict set of rules. Obviously, there is a lot of mysteries surrounding it, but that what I want. I want my players to feel some personal horror in the course of the chronicle, since so far only one truly endured it during his Prologue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more like a Nemesis with a thing for using peoples dark secrets against them rather than a Collector. Nemeses are all about punishing people for the things they've done. A Collector feeds from the shock of having something precious stolen from you while a Nemesis feeds from the shock of being punished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:57:21-08:00","id":774022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/772928-what-kind-of-beasts-do-exists?p=774010#post774010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like a Nemesis with a thing for using peoples dark secrets against them rather than a Collector. Nemeses are all about punishing people for the things they've done. A Collector feeds from the shock of having something precious stolen from you while a Nemesis feeds from the shock of being punished.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do still think there's room for a Collector who collects dark secrets, though. Doesn't have to actually do anything with them, just soaks up the fear caused by a target knowing that <i>someone</i> knows their secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:17:25-08:00","id":774041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/772928-what-kind-of-beasts-do-exists?p=774010#post774010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like a Nemesis with a thing for using peoples dark secrets against them rather than a Collector. Nemeses are all about punishing people for the things they've done. A Collector feeds from the shock of having something precious stolen from you while a Nemesis feeds from the shock of being punished.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The Beast Ur-Than described is more likely to be a Nemesis (Hunger for punishment) or Ravager (Hunger for ruin). You don't need to change anything about the concept, though. There is more to Beasts than just their Hungers and you came up with something really evocative. Also, if it has been the same Beast for all this time, we are dealing with one powerful entity. Probably even an Incarnate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:45:48-08:00","id":774070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/772928-what-kind-of-beasts-do-exists?p=774022#post774022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do still think there's room for a Collector who collects dark secrets, though. Doesn't have to actually do anything with them, just soaks up the fear caused by a target knowing that <i>someone</i> knows their secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who either has an Agency working for them, or towards their deaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T12:04:13-08:00","id":774179,"title":"","content":"The thing is... the only ones who knows if the Beast is the same from those ancient times are the Elders from the Nosferatu. And most of them have been lost to madness since a long time or even destroyed. There was always a Beast, however, but perhaps it is a &quot;nest&quot; of them, or perhaps it is always the same. But I'll change it from Collector to Nemesis then. In any cases, its power is great it has allies in the Nosferatu and possibly others denizens of the World of Darkness (I don't want to give it too much ties, but the local Circle of the Crone, known as the Cult of Epona probably has approximate knowledge of the Beasts, if not this one precisely).<br /> <br /> With this one, still, I can already began to push more layers of complexity behind the &quot;mundane&quot; unlife of Vampires in a mostly secular Domain, which is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T05:45:54-08:00","id":775413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/772928-what-kind-of-beasts-do-exists?p=773692#post773692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Eshmaki collector could be of use in my chronicle (at a very personal level for my players). If a bBeast is a collector, can it be of knowledge ? And can it enter the minds of Vampires if they let them do so ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Collectors generally get their feeds through the fact now they have something, someone else doesn't. It doesn't have to be that way, but for collecting knowledge, it might be worth considering as a Hunger for Power rather than a Hunger for Hoard.<br /> <br /> <br /> For some other parallels between types of Beast and types of vampire...<br /> <br /> The Namtaru could be said to parallel the grotesque infection of the Blood, and the way your identity rots away before it.<br /> <br /> Hungers for Power and Prey exemplify how vampires work and act.<br /> <br /> The aforementioned Eshmaki with a yen for knowledge could also be an Ugallu. Ugallu have the vantage; you're exposed to their sight, and they can take you at any time. Secrets can be seen through that lens. Either version is a good Mekhet parallel.<br /> <br /> If you want to parallel the Daeva, you could have an Makara with a face to drown in, whose Hunger for Hoard revolves around lovers.<br /> <br /> The wild abandon of the Circle of the Crone might be evoked by a Hunger for Ruin; if their rites are bloody and lurid they might hang with a Namtaru, while if they're primal and overwhelming they might hang with an Anakim, and if they're easy to get lost in they might hang with the Makara.<br /> <br /> If the Invictus are mighty, they might parallel the Anakim. If they're pervasive, they might parallel the Eshmaki. If they're distant and sudden in action, they might parallel the Ugallu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/772928-what-kind-of-beasts-do-exists?p=773839#post773839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not exactly what I meant. Beasts victimize Mortals to feed their Hungers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something to add here. Beasts could in theory feed on vampires (and other supernaturals) as well, but it's a less filling and satisfying meal. (Conversely, vampires can drink Beast blood, though the book doesn't say what unusual effects it might have).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 11-27-2015, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}